# The Graphiti image's Python dependencies. requirements.txt pins every package with its hashes; it
# is compiled in this directory with uv 0.7.2 by the command its header records.
#
# graphiti-core 0.31.2 with its anthropic extra, and every package that it installs at the version
# that graphiti-core's own uv.lock pins at that release (the uv.lock of its source distribution,
# graphiti_core-0.31.2.tar.gz), so that the image runs Graphiti as its release was tested. That lock
# pins anthropic 0.111.0, of the SDK's 0.x line: Graphiti's AnthropicClient passes `temperature` on
# every call, which anthropic 1.0.0 removed from messages.create, so with anthropic 1.0 or later
# every call it makes raises TypeError. On 0.x the adapter sets that temperature to the SDK's omit
# sentinel, and the SDK leaves it out of the request.
graphiti-core[anthropic]==0.31.2
